WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.140
Before Senator and Former Attorney General of California Kamala Harris

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.280
was chosen as Joe Biden's running mate in the 2020 election,

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.160
she played a role in a campaign to force a website called Backpage.com

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.320
to stop operating on the grounds that it was used to facilitate sex trafficking.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:21.900
Backpage.com needs to shut itself down when it has created as its business model

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.920
the profiting of the selling of human beings and the purchase of human beings.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.560
Good businesses such as Craigslist understood how it could be misabused and mishandled,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.400
and they shut that aspect of their business model down.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.160
Backpage needs to do the same.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.700
We didn't kowtow, we don't tattle tale.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:46.540
It would give the lie to our entire lives our entire career of being journalists

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.760
if the government could come in and put their stubby little fingers in our chest

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.980
and make us ask for our mommy. It ain't gonna happen.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.480
In the course of her prosecution of Backpage's founders Michael Lacey and James Larkin,

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.479
Harris spread misinformation about its practices she co-filed criminal charges

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:07.600
that were quickly dismissed but
succeeded at garnering headlines and

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.840
photo ops that raised her political
profile

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.600
in reality backpage.com had become a
powerful tool for law enforcement to

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.400
catch sex traffickers
because of the cooperation and

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.720
commitment of the site's founders to the
cause

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.159
whom harris and many other state
attorneys general and politicians

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:28.400
had painted as villains backpage.com
is nothing more than a front for pimps

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.720
and
child sex traffickers to stop this

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.240
online child sex trafficking that's
being facilitated by sites

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.000
such as this harris had supported
anti-sex trafficking bills when she was

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.759
district attorney of san francisco but
it was in october 2016

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:45.040
after she was elected california
attorney general that she co-filed

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.280
criminal charges against lacey and
larkin

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.360
as well as backpage ceo carl farrar
though accused of running a website used

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.040
by sex traffickers the charges were
quickly tossed out because lacey and

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.200
larkin were clearly protected by section
230 of the communications decency act

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.719
known as the internet's first amendment
which says that an online platform

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:06.240
isn't responsible for many types of
content posted by its customers

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.679
according to lacie and larkin the
charges were so thin there was no reason

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:12.319
to file them
except as a stunt to raise her public

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:17.840
profile she does this
right before the election and inside the

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:23.360
courtroom there was a jail cell
they filmed us in the jail cell

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.440
and then broadcast it on the evening
news

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.640
so harris gets to have her name in all
the papers right before the election

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.840
saying that she's the one who helped
take down these people that everyone for

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.239
years has been characterizing as
these big evil sex traffickers it was a

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:41.280
publicity stunt
lacie and larkin spent four days in a

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.319
sacramento jail
she knew the section 230 barred her from

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:46.480
bringing these charges but she brought
them anyway

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.840
and of course a judge threw them right
out so harris filed another set of

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.280
charges against the three men
harris was trying to say that drawer and

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.959
lacie and larkin by virtue of having
this sight and knowing that sometimes

00:02:56.959 --> 00:02:59.519
you know
bad things happen there that they were

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:02.720
guilty these other pimping charges later
get dismissed too

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.680
journalist elizabeth nolan brown writes
about sex workers in the criminal

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.879
justice system and she's been covering
the lawsuit against backpage

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:12.560
which recently got rescheduled to 2021
because of covet 19.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.400
brown revealed secret justice department
memos showing prosecutors spent years

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.360
trying to build a child sex trafficking
case against backpage

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.560
but failed to uncover compelling
evidence of criminal intent

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.680
or pattern or reckless conduct regarding
minors

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.599
instead justice department officials
found backpage was remarkably responsive

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:32.959
to law enforcement requests
and proactively sent ads containing

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:36.319
minors to authorities
the memos revealed a world far outside

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:39.840
the characterization harris and other
politicians attorneys general

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.879
and activists had been pushing for years
about backpage

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:46.480
to be clear this is a crime it is a
crime

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.080
that is rightly punishable by
incarceration

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.799
in prison on january 10 2017
harris who had been elected the junior

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:58.560
senator from california participated in
hearings on backpage

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.879
these individuals must be held
accountable these allegations must be

00:04:02.879 --> 00:04:06.000
given
voice and we have to do all that is

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.200
right to make sure that we as a civil
society

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.840
protect always the most vulnerable among
us and not take advantage of them

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.919
assuming nobody will care these hearings
have made clear

00:04:17.919 --> 00:04:22.320
we care but as harris and other senators
characterized backpage as complicit in

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.199
sex trafficking
justice department memos revealed law

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:29.040
enforcement officers the country over
were working with backpage employees

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.040
taking seminars on how to use the site
from backpage lawyers and coming to rely

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.440
on the site for sex trafficking
investigations

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.680
a 2012 memo described the backpage data
as a goldmine of information for

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.800
investigators
so many different people put on this

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.080
huge show of making them the villain in
this

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.360
a lot of people in government actively
made the calculation to

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.840
make life more dangerous for both sex
workers and sex trafficking victims

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.600
in order to satisfy this crusade that
they were on publicly

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.080
on april 6 2018 the fbi raided the homes
of lacey and larkin

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.680
and accused them of running a website
that facilitated prostitution their

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.800
trial is scheduled to take place in
january 2021.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.560
it's hard to make us feel guilty we're
not guilty

